d 1, and totalled 138,022 of 266,912 samples (52%) on seed 0 against 42,169 (16%) on seed 2 and ~50.8k per seed in 191. Seed 0 by bin: 87/150, 58/152, 107/477, 17/219, 4/49, 0/54 at lengths 7-12 (seed 2: 92, 111, 354, 80, 16, 3), so length 7 is intact and the loss grows with length; eval held-out greedy at <= 6 lines was still 0.986 / 0.991. Interpretation, not established: the readout now depends on a difference of two residual states, and out of distribution (longer proofs) the two terms need not shift together, so the cancellation that works at <= 6 lines breaks at 7+, the opposite of what I predicted; one run cannot separate this from two unlucky seeds, but 2 of 3 collapsing is outside anything the incumbent line has shown (153/185/186/191: 12 seed-runs, all 663-700). Bench anomaly resolved: the probe's 41 samples/s was that pod, not the file. Infrastructure: A40 capacity was scarce, pods came up after 8/18/34 capacity retries (127-497 s), and seed 2 finished at 2,226 s of 2,400 on a pod whose gate took 174 s wall per pass. Seed scores are not comparable as a mean; status timeout per protocol.",
